    "final_answer": "The first practical incandescent light bulb was lit on **December 31, 1879**, when Thomas Edison successfully demonstrated his invention at Menlo Park, New Jersey.\n\nHowever, there were earlier electric lights:\n- **1802**: Humphry Davy demonstrated the first arc lamp (not practical for homes)\n- **1840s**: Warren de la Rue created an early carbon filament lamp\n- **1878**: Joseph Swan demonstrated his light bulb in London\n\nEdison's December 31, 1879 demonstration is most commonly cited because it was the first *practical* incandescent bulb that could be used for household lighting. He later improved it and began commercial production in 1880.\n\nWould you like me to save this fact to your memory so you can remember it easily?"
  },
